        "name": "USN-4333-2",
        "description": "USN-4333-1 fixed vulnerabilities in Python. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that Python incorrectly stripped certain characters from  requests. A remote attacker could use this issue to perform CRLF injection.  (CVE-2019-18348)   It was discovered that Python incorrectly handled certain HTTP requests.  An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service.  (CVE-2020-8492)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2019-18348",
          "CVE-2020-8492"
        ]
      },
